# manual checks of sign-in (Rider, Visual Studio or the VS Code REST Client); the seed makes user-1 ... user-5
# with the password Seed__UserPassword of .env, each with one device whose id is the user id (the userId of the
# answer of /auth/login); the cookie of the panel is Secure, so use the https profile of the api
@host = https://localhost:7105
@password = change-me-1
@deviceId = paste-the-user-id
@code = paste-a-code
@refreshToken = paste-a-refresh-token
@accessToken = paste-an-access-token

### sign in the account panel: the answer sets the cookie dara.account (no token in the body)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "login": "user-1", "password": "{{password}}" }

### the panel issues a one-time code for its device (10 minutes, a new one replaces the old one)
POST {{host}}/account/devices/{{deviceId}}/login-code

### the device signs in with the code: device tokens and the device id
POST {{host}}/auth/device-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{code}}" }

### refresh the device tokens: the old refresh token is used up
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

### sign out the device
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### sign out the panel: the session ends and the cookie is removed
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
